`frame->rows`, continuation §2.7).\n   316\t\n   317\t### 5.3 Pending (content rows)\n   668\t6. **Canonical numbering.** Recompute §6 under the work bound and\n   669\t   compare (`:yin.k/undecodable`, kind `:noncanonical-cells`; or the\n   670\t   resource refusal of §10.10 if the bound is exceeded).\n   671\t7. **Frames.** Every `:act`, `:tail`, `:kframe`, `:reified` and\n   672\t   parked-table state is decoded to its keyed frame and judged by\n   673\t   `yin.vm.semantic-register.frame/defect` with its context (`:wait`,\n   674\t   `:captured`, `:parked`) and the decoded task context (parked key, live\n   675\t   FFI call ids, the root's free environment); a defect is\n   676\t   `:yin.k/undecodable` with the rule's kind and the row path\n   677\t   (continuation §3). This step runs after canonical numbering (step 6)\n   678\t   and before pending validation (step 8).\n   679\t8. **Pending and operations.** Reason-specific slot rules; correlation\n   680\t   agreement of §5.3 (cell stream, envelope ids, module names); every\n   681\t   op-id below `next-op-seq`, unique across the tree, absent without\n   682\t   origin; every install response verified as §5.4 requires.\n   683\t9. **Dependency closure.** Compute the census of amendment §6 from the\n   684\t   rows (waits, pendings and envelopes, parked records, store, module\n   685\t   stores, result, children) and require the carried `requires` and\n   686\t   `code` map to agree with it exactly: a declared segment not reached\n   687\t   or a reached segment not declared is `:yin.k/undecodable`. Then\n   688\t   evaluate `requires` per UCF §7.6.5: missing segments, primitives,\n   689\t   modules, streams, cursor profiles are `:yin.k/unsatisfied`; a body\n   690\t   with cells claims `:dao.stream.remote/v1`; module-store coverage is\n   691\t   complete for every `store-of` reached.\n   692\t10. **Custody.** For an exclusive root, the occurrence, baseline and\n   693\t    operation inspector and admission checks of §7.7.8; an authority\n  1088\t+----------------------+----------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n  1089\t| semantic,            | row set              | `lower` (§5.2) then the row above; composed by the composition exactly as `linearize/ast-loader` is today                |\n  1090\t| AST medium           |                      | (`linearize.cljc:269-286`, chosen in `src/cljc/yin/repl/core.cljc:63-68`)                                             |\n  1091\t+----------------------+----------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n  1092\t\n  1093\tDatom-batch loading is the projection path: a batch of `:yin/*` datoms is\n  1094\tprojected to rows by the datom→row half of the §9.1 codec pair and then\n  1095\tloaded as above; a batch of `:yin.code/*` datoms is decoded to a vector\n  1096\tby UCF §7.3.4's projection rule and then loaded as above. The projection\n  1097\tpath exists for media that carry datoms and for the datom projection of\n  1098\t§6.5; it is not a second loader and it runs the same validator (§7.2).\n  1099\t\n  1100\t### 7.2 Conformance: one validator, one image\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.md:23:§4.2 (row names `:act`/`:tail`, root `free-env`, the pure frame\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.md:718:rd]`; `:stack` and `stack-base` are removed; the root gains `free-env`,\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.md:951:stated precisely (§6.1.3: the 26 B0 rows and twelve register-corpus\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.md:953:explicit zero-argument bridge; §6.1.4: ten C4 root import programs to\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.md:1105:   install-child gate (derivations design §6.1.4 (c)); finalize\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:1459:The fixed point starts from the frame, its K frames, the parked records of\n### 6.1 Code\n\n**DECIDED** (rulings 1, 3, 4; phase-5 §7.6, §9.2; v2 amendment §4's\n2026-10-10 note). The root's `code` slot is plain `{A canonical-vector}`\nof `\"v4\"` vectors, verified to hash to their key and to pass\n`code/well-formed?`. **No native image travels**: a stack or register\nreceiver derives `H(A)`/`R(A)` with `derive/stack-image`/`register-image`.\n`requires` carries UCF §7.6.1's map **plus** `:yin.k/trees {A #{tree-address …}}`,\none entry per address in `:yin.k/segments`; the **complete association\nrule** is phase-5's: an absent entry **or an empty set** is incomplete\n(`:yin.k/missing :yin.k/trees`, discovery `:incomplete`), and a claimed\naddress alone does not establish retrievability (a known address whose\nread fails now is the medium's `:absent`, not a missing association).\n\n### 6.2 Rows, not datoms\n### 7.1 Lift\n\n**DECIDED** (draft §9, UCF §7.8): refuse unless quiescent; refuse the\nholds (`unliftable-hold`, `handoff.cljc:588`) as `:yin.k/non-portable\n:reason-mismatch`; classify kind; run the **dependency closure over the\n`\"v4\"` vectors**, which needs the phase-5 scanners\n(`scan/requirements`, `scan/free-names`, `scan/free-occurrences` over the\n§2.3 table: the current `completion/code-facts` reads stack-table\npositions and cannot be used), and refuse `:yin.k/unsatisfied` unless\n`:complete`, `:yin.k/trees` included; number cells (draft §6); walk\nwaits, parked records, the store slice, module stores, the free\nenvironment (from the kernel's `:free-env` field or the lift's explicit\n`:free-env` argument, §6.3, never from a current `E`), the result,\ninstall children; run `frame/defect` over every\nframe; emit rows and the census. A de Bruijn source walks the frames\n`layout/lift-act`/`lift-tail` reconstruct.\n\n### 7.2 Lower\n\n**DECIDED** (draft §8 in order; §3.3): gate, structure, graph, hashes,\ncanonical form, canonical numbering, **frames**, pending and operations,\ndependency closure (`requires`/`code` agree with the census;\n`:yin.k/trees` complete per §6.1), custody, composition, restore. Restore\nbuilds the receiving kernel's state: semantic-register: `code` through\n`load-vector`/`attach-image` under `code/contract`, the free environment\nas base `:env`, each `:wait` to an engine entry (payload plus the\npending's engine fields, `lower-frame!`'s shapes, `handoff.cljc:3182-3246`,\n`:deliver` carried), parked records into `:parked`, the result into\n`:value`; de Bruijn: derive and attach the image for each A, set\n`:free-env`, and `layout/lower-act`/`lower-tail` each frame (the stack\nlane's `tail` needs 6c-pre). Restoration delivers nothing, runs nothing,\nmints nothing.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Slices, gates, entry conditions\n**F13 — §9 \"Corpora\" (ACCEPT WITH CHANGES).** Replace \"H and R goldens\nare preserved only if §8.4 says the bytes held.\" with \"R and H goldens\nare the new lowerers' own, pinned at the slices and re-pinned at cutover\nwhen the descriptors lose their lift declaration (derivations design\n§8.1-8.2); neither is compared with an earlier image.\"\n\n**F14 — §10 phase 8 (ACCEPT WITH CHANGES).** After \"remove the old H/R\nrequest paths and the `raise` dependency,\" insert \"remove the\n`:dim/lift-to` row from both de Bruijn descriptors without a version\nbump and regenerate the descriptor hashes and every pinned H and R\n(derivations design §8.1-8.2); delete `yin.vm.debruijn-resolve`,\n`yin.vm.debruijn-linearize`, `yin.vm.debruijn-register-compile` and their\ntests only after the replacement coverage of §8.4 is green and the\ndescriptor-hash golden has moved to a surviving namespace; switch\n`linker/relowered`, `publish-closure!` and the REPL to the A-derived\nlowerings (§8.3); regenerate the manifests' derivation records as\n`A → H`, `A → R` and the format index in its final shape\n`{format storage-address}` (§7.6, §8.1); run the C4 suite over the newly\npublished images as the install-child gate (§6.1.4 (c))\".\n\n### 9.2 Statements that conflict with the unitarity invariant\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
